UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Seven of Swords represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Stealth"—the tactical, low-visibility phase where the sovereign consciousness, realizing that its current environment is fundamentally hostile to its integrity, chooses to "extract" its most vital resources rather than engage in a direct, likely futile, confrontation. Moving beyond the orderly transit of the Six, the Seven signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Extraction," where you are operating with strategic cunning, prioritizing the survival of your vision over the egoic need for an open battle. Visually depicted as a figure sneaking away from a camp with five swords, leaving two behind, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Discretion"—the realization that true power is the ability to recognize when the manifest environment is not currently conducive to your truth, and having the tactical flexibility to "slip out" with your core components intact. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Resource Recovery," where you are reclaiming the intellectual or creative assets that you previously surrendered to a system that was not valuing them. When the Seven of Swords appears, your system is registering a "Strategic Withdrawal" status; you are currently in a compromised position, and you are being invited to stop the "transparent struggle" and instead utilize your intelligence to optimize for your long-term viability. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your transparency. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Discretion": identifying what is truly yours, what must be left behind to maintain your cover, and executing a precise, surgical exit that allows you to live to fight another day. To inhabit the Seven of Swords is to master the art of "Strategic Cunning," recognizing that by choosing to move with intelligence rather than force, you are not acting with cowardice, but with a highly advanced, protective, and sovereign form of survivalism.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Seven of Swords appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Exposure," "Extraction-Failure," or the catastrophic refusal to recognize that your attempts at "stealth" have actually become a self-sabotaging, deceptive, and ultimately transparent strategy that is actively eroding your integrity—a state where you are effectively "running a con" on yourself. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "getting away with it" with "being clever," even as you realize your internal operating system is in a state of total, compromised transparency. You are essentially "carrying a broken bundle," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to "outsmart the system" over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually build a stable, honest foundation. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "master strategist," while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of shame, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency anxiety, the experience of "being found out," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your "clever" maneuvers are the primary cause of your own, systemic instability. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of evasion"; you are obsessively trying to hide your true intent, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final abandonment of this failing tactic is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to drop the "stealth" and stand in the open, you would be forced to acknowledge that your current position is fundamentally indefensible. The reversed Seven of Swords exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of "being honest about your limitations," and the corresponding fear that if you were to stop the deceptive posturing and act with integrity, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these manipulative, evasive scripts, perform a brutal audit of your strategic honesty, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize the integrity of your process over the utility of your schemes. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dissonance, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical transparency—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "the trick" over the vulnerability of "the truth," and realizing that until you are willing to lay the swords down, face your opponents (or your reality) directly, and accept the consequences of an honest stand, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom advantage you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 35;
